<#--
  Canadian supplemented food facts table, SOR/2022-143.

  It is the nutrition facts table of B.01.401 with two differences the regulation states: its own
  title, and a closing block declaring the ingredients the food was supplemented with. Everything
  else — the rounding, the order of the nutrients, the daily values — is that of the standard
  table, which is why this template only adds to the Canadian body rather than drawing its own.

  The caption of the block carries the mark the closing note explains: the amount declared for an
  ingredient covers its naturally occurring amount as well.

  A nutrient enters the block by being marked as a supplemental ingredient on its line of the
  nutrition list, provided the List of Permitted Supplemental Ingredients names it, and leaves the
  table for it even when it is a core nutrient. The block declares nothing else, in the order of
  that list.
-->
<#import "nutritionFacts-lib.ftlx" as nf>
<#assign W = nf.canadianWidth(nf_data, nf_data.isBilingual()?then(180, 162)) in nf>

<#assign y = nf.BORDER + 2>
<#assign body>

	<@nf.canadianHeading data=nf_data y=y titleKey="supplementedTitle" titleSize=nf.fittedTitleSize(nf_data, "supplementedTitle", 13)/>
	<#assign y = nf.cursorY>

	<@nf.canadianBody data=nf_data y=y withSupplemental=true/>
</#assign>
<@nf.panel height=nf.cursorY>${body}</@nf.panel>
